[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64924,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Clear cell carcinoma (CCC) is a malignant glandular tumour with tubulocystic, papillary, or solid patterns, often with cells with clear cytoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64925,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8310/3 Clear cell adenocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64926,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C71.0 &amp; XH6L02 Adenocarcinoma of vagina &amp; Clear cell adenocarcinoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64927,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64928,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64929,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This tumour is most commonly localized in the anterior wall of the upper third of the vagina.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64930,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "<p>CCCs of the vagina were previously seen mostly in young women, in association with in&nbsp;utero diethylstilbestrol (DES) exposure, but they are now more commonly seen in older women independent of DES exposure {4636892; 4857957; 851158}. The tumours usually present with vaginal bleeding or discharge.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-26T14:49:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64931,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These are rare primary vaginal neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64932,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Previously, most primary vaginal CCCs arose in association with adenosis in women exposed to DES in&nbsp;utero. Since the discontinuation of DES use during pregnancy, the incidence of vaginal CCCs has markedly declined. Non&ndash;DES-associated neoplasms may occur in association with adenosis or endometriosis, or without an identifiable precursor.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64933,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64934,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>They most commonly form a polypoid, exophytic mass but may be flat and ulcerated.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64935,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histological features are similar to those of the corresponding tumours elsewhere in the gynaecological tract, with tubulocystic, papillary, and solid arrangements of cells with clear or eosinophilic cytoplasm. Stromal hyalinization, eosinophilic hyaline globules, and hobnail cells are sometimes seen. Vaginal CCCs tend to have a predominant tubulocystic pattern and hobnail cells. The immunophenotype is identical to that of CCCs at other sites in the gynaecological tract, often with positive staining for napsin&nbsp;A and HNF1&beta; {29901522}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64936,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vaginal smears are effective for early detection of vaginal CCC. Specific vaginal sampling must be performed; cervical-only sampling is not sufficient {10600286}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64937,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64938,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> malignant glandular tumour with tubulocystic, papillary, or solid patterns, often with cells with clear cytoplasm.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64939,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other vaginal carcinomas.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64940,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 346,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrence occurs in about 25% of cases. The 10-year overall survival rate for all stages is 80% for DES-related cases but only 60% for non&ndash;DES-related cases {7959291}. Favourable prognosis is seen with low stage, younger age, smaller size, minimal stromal invasion, and a tubulocystic pattern.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:09:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]